.Dd September 13, 2026
.Dt SQUEUE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm squeue_init ,
.Nm squeue_exit ,
.Nm squeue_get_sqe ,
.Nm squeue_submit ,
.Nm squeue_submit_and_wait ,
.Nm squeue_peek_cqe ,
.Nm squeue_wait_cqe ,
.Nm squeue_cqe_seen
.Nd ergonomic interface to the squeue completion-ring engine
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libsqueue
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In squeue.h
.Ft int
.Fn squeue_init "struct squeue *q" "unsigned entries"
.Ft void
.Fn squeue_exit "struct squeue *q"
.Ft struct io_uring_sqe *
.Fn squeue_get_sqe "struct squeue *q"
.Ft int
.Fn squeue_submit "struct squeue *q"
.Ft int
.Fn squeue_submit_and_wait "struct squeue *q" "unsigned wait_nr"
.Ft int
.Fn squeue_wait_cqe "struct squeue *q" "struct io_uring_cqe **cqep"
.Ft "struct io_uring_cqe *"
.Fn squeue_peek_cqe "struct squeue *q"
.Ft void
.Fn squeue_cqe_seen "struct squeue *q" "struct io_uring_cqe *cqe"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm libsqueue
wraps the
.Xr squeue 2
system calls and shared rings so an application can submit and reap
asynchronous I/O without managing the ring mappings and head/tail indices by
hand.  It is header-only: every function is inline in
.In squeue.h ,
and linking
.Fl l Ns Ar squeue
is only needed for the version accessors.
.Pp
.Fn squeue_init
creates a ring of at least
.Fa entries
submission slots and maps its regions into
.Fa q .
.Fn squeue_exit
unmaps the regions and closes the ring.
.Pp
To issue work, obtain a submission entry with
.Fn squeue_get_sqe
(returns
.Dv NULL
if the ring is full), fill it with a
.Fn squeue_prep_ *
helper
.Pq Fn squeue_prep_nop , Fn squeue_prep_read , Fn squeue_prep_write ,
.Fn squeue_prep_readv , Fn squeue_prep_writev , Fn squeue_prep_fsync ,
.Fn squeue_prep_poll_add ,
optionally attach user data with
.Fn squeue_sqe_set_data ,
then publish with
.Fn squeue_submit
or, to also block for completions,
.Fn squeue_submit_and_wait .
.Pp
Reap completions with
.Fn squeue_peek_cqe
(non-blocking) or
.Fn squeue_wait_cqe
(blocking), read the
.Fa res
and
.Fa user_data
fields, and release each with
.Fn squeue_cqe_seen .
Files, buffers and an eventfd may be registered with
.Fn squeue_register_files ,
.Fn squeue_register_buffers
and
.Fn squeue_register_eventfd .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn squeue_init ,
.Fn squeue_submit ,
.Fn squeue_submit_and_wait
and
.Fn squeue_wait_cqe
return 0 (or a non-negative count) on success, or a negative
.Va errno
on failure.
.Fn squeue_get_sqe
and
.Fn squeue_peek_cqe
return
.Dv NULL
when no slot or completion is available.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr squeue 2
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm libsqueue
first appeared in 5BSD.
